hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1423","Narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sana'ani, narrated by al-Mu'tamir, who said: I heard Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He delivered a sermon on Friday, and the people stood up to him and shouted, saying: O Prophet of God, the rain has fallen, the trees have turned red, and the livestock have perished, so pray to God. To give us water, so he said: “O God, give us water, O God, give us water.” He said: By God, we do not see in the sky a speck of a cloud, and a cloud arose and spread, then It rained, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came down, prayed, and left. It did not stop raining until the next Friday. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, rose He, peace and blessings be upon him, was delivering a sermon. They shouted and said: O Prophet of God, the houses have been destroyed and the paths have been cut off, so pray to God to withhold them from us. He said: Then he smiled, And he said: “O God, protect us or against us.” He said: Then it dispersed from the city, and it started raining around it, but it did not rain in the city a drop. He said: Then I looked at the city, and it was like a crown."
